# 26. GENERATION FAILURE HANDLING

Define predictable behavior.

### AI provider failure

Use bounded retry where appropriate.

### Malformed JSON

Use existing JSON repair/validation mechanisms where appropriate.

### Invalid course structure

Reject or regenerate.

### Duplicate modules

Regenerate/revise.

### Resource failure

Do not fail the entire course unnecessarily.

### YouTube failure

Course should still be usable.

### PDF/resource failure

Course should still be usable.

### MongoDB failure

Do not claim that the Course was saved.

The user should clearly know:

```text
Course generated successfully.
Saving failed.
Please retry.
```

Do not silently pretend persistence succeeded.

